@baseUrl=http://localhost:8000/api/v1/payments
@paymentId=REPLACE_WITH_PAYMENT_ID
@retailerToken=REPLACE_WITH_RETAILER_ACCESS_TOKEN
@adminToken=REPLACE_WITH_ADMIN_ACCESS_TOKEN

# No POST / — a Payment is only ever created as a side effect of
# POST /participants (see pool.participants.http / 00-smooth-flow.http),
# which also returns the Thawani checkoutUrl to redirect the retailer to.
# No PATCH /:id either — every transition below is a dedicated action tied
# to an actual Thawani confirmation, not a generic field write.

### list my own payments (RETAILER)

GET {{baseUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{retailerToken}}

### list every payment (ADMIN)

GET {{baseUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### get a specific payment (owner, or ADMIN for any)

GET {{baseUrl}}/{{paymentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{retailerToken}}

### confirm payment status against Thawani (owner or ADMIN) — this is what
### the frontend calls when the retailer lands back on success_url; only a
### 'paid' Thawani session moves the payment to COMPLETED and the
### participation to WAITING

POST {{baseUrl}}/{{paymentId}}/confirm
Authorization: Bearer {{retailerToken}}

### cancel a still-PENDING payment (owner or ADMIN) — this is what the
### frontend calls when the retailer lands on cancel_url, or what an admin
### does to clear a session nobody ever returned to; releases the pool's
### quantity reservation if the pool is still OPEN

POST {{baseUrl}}/{{paymentId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{retailerToken}}

### retry a refund request that previously failed (ADMIN only, from
### REFUND_FAILED)

POST {{baseUrl}}/{{paymentId}}/retry-refund
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### manually confirm a refund actually completed (ADMIN only, from
### REFUND_PENDING) — a deliberate human step, not an automatic poll; see
### thawani.gateway.ts for why

POST {{baseUrl}}/{{paymentId}}/confirm-refund
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
